      shapes whose `pos-v2` / `pos` literals are intrinsic to
      what the tool detects.

  - NEW sibling migration helper:
      framework/tools/loam-migrate-launchd-labels/
      (parallel structure to M1b's loam-migrate-host-config/).
      One-shot per-host bootout-of-old + rename-aside flow:
        * Scan ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ for com.pos-v2.<2segments>.plist
        * launchctl bootout gui/<uid>/<label> (benign-stderr-as-success)
        * Rename the plist to <base>.label-rebrand-disabled.bak
      Idempotent: re-run after success finds zero matches.
      Out of scope for the helper:
        * pre-#6 single-segment orphans (orphan-plist-cleanup's
          mission)
        * writing new com.loam.<slug>.<kind>.plist files
          (workspace-bootstrap first-run scaffold owns that)

